GLB, Canada's energy transport company with transportation and storage operations in the United States, Gulf of Mexico, the Arctic, Alaska and Latin America. GLB operates under several business lines: GLBCO, Global Clean Marine, the Tankers Division, the Oil Companies Billions, GLBS Offshore Services LLC [Gloucester, Massachusetts], IAG Ship Management, New Millennium LNG and Global Gas Logistics Ltd.
This profile is not a complete description of Globus. It is updated as such when new financial information becomes available.
Global Gas Logistics Ltd., or GLBS Off Shore Services ("GS"), was created to own and operate offshore gas sales platform owned interests and other related offshore structures in order to allow management greater flexibility to pursue longer-term opportunities. To manage its corporate affiliates, GLBS works closely with the global merchant trading companies for which it provides services, including:
Vales Shipping Pte Ltd (VL Shipping);
Van Der Nat Corporation;
Van Der Nat (NL), a wholly-owned Singapore subsidiary of VLShipping

