1.1 Mathematical skills and reasoning
At the end of Level 2, candidates must be able to demonstrate a mastery of the skills and techniques in:
• arithmetic (using mental arithmetic without using calculators)
• algebra
• geometry
at Levels M and C.
At this level, the candidate is considered competent if he/she can:
• subtract whole numbers up to 1000; reduce fractions to simplest form;
• perform elementary problem solving by deduction; solve geometric problems concerning
areas, perimeters and volumes ;and problems involving compound quantities;
• add, subtract, multiply, divide, distribute and carry out scientific calculations ;factor expressions;
• recognise products and composition;
• recognise angles and use basic conic graphs;
• solve equations involving polynomial expressions and radicals;
• use powers of 10 in calculations.
